  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Find all integer values of $b$ for which $x^2+bx-7$ has integer roots.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$b=\\pm6$.",
      "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^2+bx-7$. By the Integer Root Theorem, any integer root must be one of $\\pm1,\\pm7$.\n\nTesting each possible root:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1+b-7=0\\\\b&=6\\\\P(-1)&=1-b-7=0\\\\b&=-6\\\\P(7)&=49+7b-7=0\\\\b&=-6\\\\P(-7)&=49-7b-7=0\\\\b&=6\\end{align*}$$\nFor $b=6$, $P(x)=(x-1)(x+7)$, with integer roots $1,-7$.\n\nFor $b=-6$, $P(x)=(x+1)(x-7)$, with integer roots $-1,7$.\n\nTherefore, $b=\\pm6$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
